                    \\,.
          %h3#Pi0InLocConTop
            Geometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
            of a general object in a locally connected topos
          %p
            More generally, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+connected+topos"} locally connected topos
            then the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ←
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (LConst \dashv \Gamma) : E \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\to} Set
            has also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_0
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LConst
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LConst
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi E
                  %mover
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi Γ
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi LConst
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 0
                  %mi Set
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi_0 \dashv LConst \dashv \Gamma) :
                  E \stackrel{\overset{\Pi_0}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{LConst}{\leftarrow}}{\overset{\Gamma}{\to}}}
                  Set
                  \\,.
          %p For instance page 17 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              %em Classifying Spaces and Classifying Topoi
              Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1616, Springer (1995)
          %h3#geometric__of_objects_in_a_1topos
            Geometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1
            of objects in a 1-topos
          %p The general idea is that of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck%27s+Galois+theory"}> Grothendieck's Galois theory
              \.
          %p
            A discussion of of how this produces first homotopy groups of a 1-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            is at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+group+of+a+topos"}> fundamental group of a topos
              \.
          %p
            The general construction of the first geometric homotopy group of objects in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            is for instance in section 8.4 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em Topos theory
              \.
          %h3#geometric__of_a_topological_space
            Geometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_2
            of a topological space
          %p This case is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pietro+Polesello"} Pietro Polesello
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ingo+Waschkies"} Ingo Waschkies
              %em Higher monodromy
              , Homology, Homotopy and Applications, Vol. 7(2005), No. 1, pp. 109-150 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/HHA/v7/n1/a7/v7n1a7.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p We indicate briefly how the results stated in this article fit into the general abstract picture as indicated above:
          %p
            The authors consider locally constant 1-stacks and 2-stacks on sites of open subsets of sufficiently nice
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            Prop. 1.1.9 gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi LConst
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (LConst \dashv \Gamma) : Sh_{(2,1)}(X) \stackrel{\overset{LConst}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}} Grpd
          %p between forming constant stacks and taking global sections.
          %p
            Then prop 1.2.5, 1.2.6, culminating in
            %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/HHA/v7/n1/a7/v7n1a7.pdf#page=13"} theorem 1.2.9, p. 121
            gives (somewhat implicitly) the other adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ←
                      %mi LConst
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 1
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi_1\dashv LConst) : Op(X) \hookrightarrow Sh_{(2,1)}(X) \stackrel{\overset{\Pi_1}{\to}}{\underset{LConst}{\leftarrow}} Grpd
          %p
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LConst
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LConst
            being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+groupoid"} fundamental groupoid
            functor on representables. (Where we change a bit the perspective on the results as presented there, to amplify the pattern indicated above. For instance where the authors write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(X,C_X)
            we think of this here equivalently as
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi LConst
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(2,1)}(X)(X,LConst(C))
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots \simeq Grpd(\Pi_1(X),C)
          %p
            Then in essentially verbatim analogy, these results are lifted from stacks to 2-stacks in section 2, where now prop 2.2.2, 2.2.3, culminating in
            %a{:href => "http://www.intlpress.com/HHA/v7/n1/a7/v7n1a7.pdf#page=24"} theorem 2.2.5, p. 132
            gives (somewhat implicitly) the adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi Op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ←
                      %mi LConst
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Π
                          %mn 2
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Pi_2\dashv LConst) : Op(X) \hookrightarrow Sh_{(3,1)}(X) \stackrel{\overset{\Pi_2}{\to}}{\underset{LConst}{\leftarrow}} Grpd
          %p
            now with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+n-groupoid"} path 2-groupoid
            operation (locally) left adjoint to forming constant 2-stacks.
          %h3#ooStackOnTopSpace
            Geometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_\infty
            of a topological space
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a sufficiently nice (I think this should be locally (relatively) contractible. -DR) (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+space"}> paracompact
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to {*}
            induces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+morphism"} geometric morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi Γ
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi LConst
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X) \stackrel{\overset{LConst}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{\Gamma}{\to}}
                  \\infty Grpd
          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            is taking
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+section"} global section
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            is forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} constant ∞-stack
            on an
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mi Core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = Core (\infty Grpd)
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi LConst
                    %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LConst_K
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} constant ∞-stack
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} locally constant ∞-stack
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi LConst
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mi LConst
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  LConst(X) := Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X, LConst_{\infty Grpd})= \Gamma LConst_{\infty Grpd}
          %p
            for the
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X) := Sing X
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .un_theorem
            %h6#claim Claim
            %p
              There is an equivalence of
              = succeed "-groupoids" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LConst
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    LConst(X) \simeq \infty Grpd(\Pi(X), \infty Grpd)
                    \\,.
          %blockquote
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              \: I think this is proven in the literature, if maybe slightly implicitly so. I’ll now go through the available references to discuss this.
          %p
            After old ideas by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
            from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pursuing+Stacks"} Pursuing Stacks
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"}> Bertrand Toen
              ,
              %em Toward a Galoisian interpretation of homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0007157"}> arXiv:0007157
              )
          %p
            In
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0007/0007157v4.pdf#page=25"} theorem 2.13, p. 25
            the author proves an equivalence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            (modeled there as
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal+category"} Segal categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Fib
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  LConst(X) \simeq Fib(\Pi(X))
          %p
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+%E2%88%9E-stack"} locally constant ∞-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Sing
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X) = Sing(X)
          %p
            But Kan fibrations over a Kan complex such as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            are equivalently
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+fibration"} left fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
            these are equivalent to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X) \to \infty Grpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-Grothendieck+construction"} (∞,1)-Grothendieck construction
            Toën’s result does actually produce an equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  LConst(X) \simeq Func(\Pi(X), \infty Grpd)
                  \\,.
          %p In
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bertrand+Toen"} Bertrand Toen
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriele+Vezzosi"} Gabriele Vezzosi
              %em Segal topoi and stacks over Segal categories
              , Proceedings of the
              %p
                Program Stacks, Intersection theory and Non-abelian Hodge Theory, MSRI, Berkeley, January-May 2002 (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0212330"}> arxiv:math/0212330
                ).
          %p
            this is discussed in the context of
            = succeed "es." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Segal-topos"} Segal-topos
          %p Very similar statements are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %em Parametrized spaces model locally constant homotopy sheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.2874"}> arXiv:0706.2874
              )
          %p and, building on that, in example 1.8 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
              ,
              %em Locally constant functors
              , Math. Proc. Camb. Phil. Soc. , 147 (
              %a{:href => "http://www-math.univ-paris13.fr/~cisinski/lcmodcat3.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A variant of this statement – more general in one respect, less general in another – appears in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
          %p
            as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0608/0608040v4.pdf#page=545"} theorem 7.1.0.1
          %p
            There it is shown that for any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \in \infty Grpd
            there is a bijection of homotopy sets of morphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0 Top(X, |K|) \simeq \pi_0(p_* p^* K)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p^* \dashv p_*) : Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X) \to \infty Grpd
            is the geometric morphism we denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi LConst
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (LConst \dashv \Gamma)
            above.
          %p
            If we also rewrite the left using
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} the equivalence
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Γ
                  %msub
                    %mi LConst
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi LConst
                    %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_0 \infty Grpd(\Pi(X), K) \simeq \pi_0(\Gamma LConst_K)
                  \= \pi_0 Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X,LConst_K)
                  \\,,
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo =
                  %mi Core
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K = Core(\infty Grpd)
            this is the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decategorification"} decategorification
            of the above statement.
          %h3#GeomPiOfTermObj
            Geometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_\infty
            of the terminal object in a locally
            = succeed "-connected" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-topos" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            The geometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_\infty
            of the terminal object in a locally ∞-connected (∞,1)-topos can be called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+%E2%88%9E-groupoid+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} fundamental ∞-groupoid
            of the topos. It
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represents
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} shape
            of the topos.
          %p On page 18-19 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"}> Ieke Moerdijk
              ,
              %em Classifying Spaces and Classifying Topoi
              Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1616, Springer (1995)
          %p
            is described the construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X) \in \infty Grpd
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
            on an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            as described above in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "PiConstruction"} Geometric fundamental oo-groupoid
          %p This reviews in particular (slightly implicitly)
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              that has a basis of contractible open subsets. Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              also for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              regarded as the terminal object in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Sh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Sh
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi : Sh_{(\infty,1)}(X) \to \infty Grpd
              has the same homtopy groups as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              regarded as an object in
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_n \Pi(X) \simeq \pi_n(X)
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p This is a slight reformulation of the statement in
            %p
              M. Artin, B. Mazur,
              %em Etale homotopy
              , Springer lecture notes in mathematics 100, Berlin 1969
          %p
            Notice the local contractibility assumption. This is necessary in general for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(X)
            to make sense.
          %h2#GeneralExamples Examples
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            and consider in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh_{(\infty,1)}(Diff)
            the two objects
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
                , the
                = succeed "-stack" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Diff
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}
                – the
                = succeed "-stack" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
                of the additive group
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p Then
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em categorical
                homotopy groups of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
                are all trivial
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                        %mi cat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\pi_n^{cat}(S^1) = {*}
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em geometric
                homotopy groups of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
                are the usual ones obtained from regarding
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
                as an object in
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                        %mi geom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\pi^{geom}_0(S^1) = *
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 1
                        %mi geom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\pi^{geom}_1(S^1) = \mathbb{Z}
              %p etc.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}
            it is the other way round:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %em categorical
                homotopy groups of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}
                are
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mi n
                        %mi cat
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi ℤ
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi if
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi n
                                %mo =
                                %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo *
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi otherwise
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\pi_n^{cat}(\mathbf{B}\mathbb{Z}) =
                      \\left\{
                      \\array{
                      \\mathbb{Z} &amp; | if\; n=1
                      \\\
                      * &amp; | otherwise
                      }
                      \\right.
                      \\,.
